    {
      "title": "Plague epidemic risk in Russia low after death of lab technician, WHO says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/06/plague-epidemic-risk-russia-low-death-darya-shipilova-who",
      "description": "<p>World Health Organization detects no sign of further outbreak since Darya Shipilova died last week</p><p>The World Health Organization has said the risk of an epidemic in Russia is low after the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/05/russia-lab-worker-possibly-dies-of-plague-siberia-quarantine-measures-irkutsk\">sudden death of a lab technician</a> who worked at a plague research institute in Siberia.</p><p>Darya Shipilova, who was 28, died last week, two days after falling ill. Russian media reports suggested she <a href=\"https://www.rferl.org/a/russia-plague-warning-siberia-irkutsk-laboratory/33870385.html\">may have become infected after an accident at her workplace</a>, where dangerous pathogens are kept and studied.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/06/plague-epidemic-risk-russia-low-death-darya-shipilova-who\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-06T23:14:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "You Probably Aren’t Going to Get the Plague",
      "link": "https://www.wired.com/story/what-we-know-about-plague-russia/",
      "description": "The death of a lab worker in Russia has authorities looking at whether plague played a role. Even if it did, though, the odds of it spreading are very low.",
      "source_name": "Wired Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-06T23:09:20"
    }
  ]
